From 4e92a9f3aa3e11518356efe016452f3d995c7fb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: airidosas252 <airidaslideikis@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:04:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] tu: keep the bottom of the separate mode ray tracing
 stack in GMEM

The stack of the separate mode lives in private memory, which goes
through the caches to DRAM. Most of the accesses are to the bottom of
the stack, so keep that part in GMEM, which is much faster, and the rest
in a BO owned by the driver. Each wave slot of each SP has a share of
both, laid out like private memory, and an access picks its base with a
select, which is cheaper than a branch around it.

A8XX keeps the CCU and VPC caches at the top of GMEM in both modes, the
stack goes below them. A thread that has no share of GMEM uses the BO
for the whole stack, so a wrong guess of the wave slots costs speed but
not correctness.

It is on for A8XX, TU_DEBUG=nogmemstack turns it off.
